  "available": true,
  "why_on_the_list": "Compounder bucket, rank 67. Forward P/E 30.6 vs a 72.3 median, 39% off its high, while procedures grew 16% last quarter. The first credible competitors in twenty years arrived, and the multiple halved.",
  "business_quality": "Razor and blade model with 11,710 da Vinci systems installed, up 12%, and surgeons trained on it for a career. Gross margin around 68 to 70%. Cash and investments $8.6 billion, no debt. Competition: Medtronic's Hugo (approved late 2025) and Johnson & Johnson's Ottava (cleared for ten general surgery procedures). Oppenheimer notes workflow problems for Ottava and footprint constraints for Hugo.",
